	(text "OUTPUT STAGE  -  3.3 V TTL UART or RS-232"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0976e224-4513-5c0a-9fba-89648a9b67df")
	)
	(text "Cisco-style console pinout, which is what an RB4011 expects:\n  1 RTS(out)  2 DTR(out)  3 TXD(out)  4 GND  5 GND\n  6 RXD(in)   7 DSR(in)   8 CTS(in)\nPins 1 and 2 are OUTPUTS of the router and are deliberately left\nunconnected - driving them would fight the router.\n \nJP6/JP7 both on 2-3 : straight patch cable to the router (default).\nJP6/JP7 both on 1-2 : rollover console cable.\nNever select the same RJ45 pin on both jumpers.\n \nJP8/JP9 are open by default; bridge them only if a device refuses\nto talk without DSR/CTS asserted.  RouterOS does not need them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 95 218 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ac67655-4a04-5116-aaff-c8883cd1f2da")
	)
	(text "J3  1 GND\n    2 TXD  (macropad -> host, idles high)\n    3 RXD  (console output monitor, via the MAX3232 receiver)\n    4 +3V3  (bus power in/out, routed through JP1)\n \nR53 is NOT fitted, and at 3.3 V it should stay that way.\nR52/R53 divide by 2k2/(1k+2k2) = 0.69, which was sized when\nthis rail was 5 V: 5 x 0.69 = 3.4 V, the number this note used\nto quote.  The rail is 3.3 V now, so fitting R53 would deliver\n2.3 V - below the 2.4 V a 3 V CMOS input wants to see, and no\nhelp to a 5 V host either.  Drive it straight through R52."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 180 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1cf75fb2-c9e0-5f78-9c34-a27c2c5ac212")
	)
	(text "JP4 is the mode selector.  Its centre pin is the live TX from the\nlogic; each outer pin feeds one output driver and is parked high by\na 10k so the unselected output sits at its idle level instead of\nfloating.\n  JP4 1-2 : RS-232 on the RJ45.  TTL header idles high.\n  JP4 2-3 : 3.3 V TTL on J3.  RS-232 driver parked at MARK.\n  JP5 (solder bridge) shorts pin 1 to pin 3 -> both outputs live."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21a4a5a4-9c6e-5a1e-a5f6-c77b41748717")
	)
	(text "RS-232 LEVEL SHIFTER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "22612447-4c5f-58fc-b4db-d5ae16e8a466")
	)
	(text "TTL UART HEADER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 130 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65ff71ce-a277-5407-826d-08c3811cc27a")
	)
	(text "MAX3232 / MAX232A: 100 nF charge-pump caps.\nA genuine MAX232 (no suffix) needs 1 uF - the\noriginal spec called for 0.1 uF with a MAX232,\nwhich will not pump."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210 145 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "68d8a2ff-d674-50e3-8c86-6ae8e0da3b97")
	)
	(text "CONSOLE PORT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
